All,



Consider guidance on the actuation of a Harco Lateral Isolation Valve.



Harco Lateral Isolation Valve actuation procedures:

*        Closing:  Turn handle in the closing direction to the point of "fi=
rst felt resistance".  Then tighten an additional 1/8th to 1/4th turn.  Do =
not tighten more than 1/4th turn past point of "first felt resistance".

*        Opening:  Turn handle in the opening direction to the point of "fi=
rst felt resistance".  At this point the seal assembly has bottomed out aga=
inst the bonnet.  Then turn handle in the closing direction 1/8th turn.  Th=
is is to provide for a gap that will prevent "sticking" of the seal assembl=
y to the bonnet.



J



Shelley:  Please file in O-Drive folder.  Edit LIV brochure to include this=
 instruction.


--_000_7972706572736767716780657968697274737676697077747373657_
